{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>They shall not harm.</b> Concerning the viper and the serpent, as though the whole land of Israel is filled with the knowledge of YHWH, for it is known that one who knows HaShem will never destroy, but only build and repair." "<b>As the waters.</b> The word אשר is missing, and so it is, for the knowledges will multiply as אשר the waters cover [the text should read: the waters that cover] the sea, without interruption, but only increase."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {1 "The bracketed Hebrew note צ״ל המים אשר יכסו is a corrected reading embedded in the manuscript tradition; I translate it as the corrected form."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:25.382290225Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}